No. Besides the 3 HTML files, you have one real feature change and one bug fix, both in `server.mjs`:

1. **`.env` support:** the server reads your API key and settings from a `.env` file. On `main` it only reads shell variables.
2. **Space-in-path fix:** on `main`, the server and one test break in any folder whose name has a space, like "EHL Final". Locally they work.

The fix is mirrored in `test/data.test.mjs`. `.env.example` and `.gitignore` support the `.env` feature, and the README has matching instructions.

The app itself is identical to `main`: no changes in `public/`, `src/` or `data/`.

The rest is presentation or notes, not app code:
- the 3 HTML files: `presentation/index.html` (new deck), `presentation/archive/v1.html` (old deck) and `bmw-product-strategy-ai.html` (not mine);
- the deck's 2 images;
- `PRODUCT.md`, `DESIGN.md`, `docs/gemini-context-brief.md`;
- `.impeccable/` (design notes and screenshots).

